/-! ## The least-congruence universal property (map-out) -/

/-- ★ **THE FOURTEEN 3-CELLS GENERATE THE IDENTIFICATION (least-congruence UP).**  For any relation
`targetRel` absorbing the distributive-law base relation (a congruence containing the strict laws and the
fourteen critical-pair rows), the two legs of EVERY critical row are `targetRel`-related — so the fourteen
generating 3-cells are the datum whose fold through `SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto` identifies each critical
pair in EVERY model.  Uniform in the row (one statement covering all fourteen, keyed on
`DistLawCriticalRow`). -/
theorem distLawCriticalPairsIdentifiedInEveryModel {targetRel : CellRelOver distLawOmegaComputad}
    (absorbs : IsSaturatedCongruenceWithId distLawOmegaComputad distLawOmegaBaseRel targetRel)
    {d : Nat} {leftLeg rightLeg : CellExpr distLawOmegaComputad d}
    (row : DistLawCriticalRow leftLeg rightLeg) : targetRel leftLeg rightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto absorbs (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr row))

